  <section class="section" id="service" aria-labelledby="service-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="service-title">The service</h2>
        <p>
          AZERTY Coach is a read-only MCP server, published by {{ mesure.coach.editeurEn }}, that you add to
          Claude, ChatGPT or Codex so that your assistant can tell you how to type a character and compare
          keyboard layouts. Its address is <code>{{ mesure.coach.url }}</code>; the
          <a href="/en/coach">help page</a> explains how to add it and what it does.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Free, no account.</strong> No payment, no registration, no key.</li>
          <li><strong>Read-only.</strong> The service returns information; it changes nothing on your computer, in your assistant or anywhere else.</li>
          <li><strong>No availability commitment.</strong> The service may be slow, interrupted, changed or stopped, without notice. We guarantee neither a response time nor a duration.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="accuracy" aria-labelledby="accuracy-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="accuracy-title">Accuracy of answers</h2>
        <p>
          The information comes from AZERTY Global data and from keyboard layouts that we check one by one, but it
          may contain errors or may not match your keyboard, your system or your software version. For a layout the
          service does not cover, it says so and does not invent keys.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your assistant writes the final answer from what the service returns. We do not control that wording.
          For any use where a typing mistake has consequences (computer code, an official document, a password),
          check the result.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

